IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `caa-types`
IMPORT `caa-convention-final`

-- Tests for the Convention, Chapters IV and V (Articles 31 to 41).  Figures read off the text:
-- the ninetieth day (Articles 37(2) and 38(3)), six months (Article 39(2)), five ratifications
-- (Article 37(2)).

§ `Tests -- Chapters IV and V`

§§ `Article 31. Combined carriage`

-- Combined Carriage Facts: partly by air and partly by another mode, the carriage by air is within Article 1, conditions for
-- another mode were inserted, the Convention is observed as regards the carriage by air.
#ASSERT `the Convention applies to the part of the carriage performed by air` (`Combined Carriage Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the Convention applies to the part of the carriage performed by air` (`Combined Carriage Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the Convention applies to the part of the carriage performed by air` (`Combined Carriage Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `the parties may insert conditions relating to the other mode of carriage` (`Combined Carriage Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the parties may insert conditions relating to the other mode of carriage` (`Combined Carriage Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the parties may insert conditions relating to the other mode of carriage` (`Combined Carriage Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE)

§§ `Article 32. Clauses infringing the Convention`

-- Clause Facts: (Article 23 fields), then infringes the Convention by law or jurisdiction, entered into before the damage,
-- an arbitration clause, carriage of cargo, arbitration within an Article 28 jurisdiction.
`a jurisdiction clause made before the damage` MEANS `Clause Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a jurisdiction clause made after the damage` MEANS `Clause Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a cargo arbitration clause within an Article 28 jurisdiction` MEANS `Clause Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE
`a cargo arbitration clause outside those jurisdictions` MEANS `Clause Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE
`a passenger arbitration clause within an Article 28 jurisdiction` MEANS `Clause Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE
`a clause that infringes nothing` MEANS `Clause Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

#ASSERT `the clause or special agreement is null and void under Article 32` `a jurisdiction clause made before the damage`
#ASSERT NOT `the clause or special agreement is null and void under Article 32` `a jurisdiction clause made after the damage`
#ASSERT NOT `the clause or special agreement is null and void under Article 32` `a cargo arbitration clause within an Article 28 jurisdiction`
#ASSERT `the clause or special agreement is null and void under Article 32` `a cargo arbitration clause outside those jurisdictions`
#ASSERT `the clause or special agreement is null and void under Article 32` `a passenger arbitration clause within an Article 28 jurisdiction`
#ASSERT NOT `the clause or special agreement is null and void under Article 32` `a clause that infringes nothing`
#ASSERT `an arbitration clause is allowed by Article 32` `a cargo arbitration clause within an Article 28 jurisdiction`
#ASSERT NOT `an arbitration clause is allowed by Article 32` `a passenger arbitration clause within an Article 28 jurisdiction`

§§ `Article 33. The carrier's freedom to refuse and to make regulations`

#ASSERT `the carrier may refuse to enter into the contract of carriage` `the Warsaw Convention` FALSE
#ASSERT `the carrier may refuse to enter into the contract of carriage` `the Warsaw Convention` TRUE
#ASSERT `the carrier may refuse to enter into the contract of carriage` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` TRUE
#ASSERT `the carrier may refuse to enter into the contract of carriage` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` FALSE
-- Third Schedule: "except as provided in paragraph (3) of Article 5"
#ASSERT NOT `the carrier may refuse to enter into the contract of carriage` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` TRUE
#ASSERT `the carrier may make the regulation` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the carrier may make the regulation` TRUE

§§ `Article 35. Days`

#ASSERT `the expression "days" means current days and not working days`

§§ `Articles 37 to 40A. Timing and status`

-- Treaty Facts: date of the fifth ratification, date of the State's ratification, date of accession notification, date of
-- denunciation notification, number of instruments deposited, ratification effective, denunciation effective.
`five ratifications deposited by 1 March 1930` MEANS `Treaty Facts` OF YMD 1930 3 1, YMD 1930 6 1, YMD 1930 7 1, YMD 1930 8 1, 5, TRUE, FALSE
`four ratifications deposited by 1 March 1930` MEANS `Treaty Facts` OF YMD 1930 3 1, YMD 1930 6 1, YMD 1930 7 1, YMD 1930 8 1, 4, TRUE, FALSE
`a State whose ratification and denunciation are both effective` MEANS `Treaty Facts` OF YMD 1930 3 1, YMD 1930 6 1, YMD 1930 7 1, YMD 1930 8 1, 5, TRUE, TRUE
`a State whose ratification is not yet effective` MEANS `Treaty Facts` OF YMD 1930 3 1, YMD 1930 6 1, YMD 1930 7 1, YMD 1930 8 1, 5, FALSE, FALSE
`a denunciation on 31 August 2025` MEANS `Treaty Facts` OF YMD 1930 3 1, YMD 1930 6 1, YMD 1930 7 1, YMD 2025 8 31, 5, TRUE, FALSE

-- 90 days after 1 March 1930 is 30 May 1930
#ASSERT `the date the Convention comes into force between the first five High Contracting Parties` `five ratifications deposited by 1 March 1930` EQUALS JUST (YMD 1930 5 30)
#ASSERT `the date the Convention comes into force between the first five High Contracting Parties` `four ratifications deposited by 1 March 1930` EQUALS NOTHING
-- 90 days after 1 June 1930 is 30 August 1930
#ASSERT `the date the Convention comes into force for a State that later deposits its ratification` `five ratifications deposited by 1 March 1930` EQUALS YMD 1930 8 30
-- 90 days after 1 July 1930 is 29 September 1930
#ASSERT `the date the accession takes effect` `five ratifications deposited by 1 March 1930` EQUALS YMD 1930 9 29
-- six months after 31 August is 28 February (the anniversary date, clamped)
#ASSERT `the date the denunciation takes effect` `a denunciation on 31 August 2025` EQUALS YMD 2026 2 28

#ASSERT `the State is a High Contracting Party` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `five ratifications deposited by 1 March 1930`
#ASSERT `the State is a High Contracting Party` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `five ratifications deposited by 1 March 1930`
#ASSERT NOT `the State is a High Contracting Party` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `a State whose ratification and denunciation are both effective`
#ASSERT NOT `the State is a High Contracting Party` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `a State whose ratification is not yet effective`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the State is a High Contracting Party` `the Warsaw Convention` `five ratifications deposited by 1 March 1930`
